---
import { bodyP, codeBlock, linkInline, proseWrap } from "./_install-tokens";
---

<div class:list={[proseWrap]}>
  <p class={bodyP}>
    It is highly recommended to add Elixir's bin path to your PATH environment
    variable to ease development.
  </p>

  <p class={bodyP}>
    On Windows, there are{" "}
    <a href="http://www.computerhope.com/issues/ch000549.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={linkInline}>instructions for different versions</a>
    {" "}explaining the process.
  </p>

  <p class={bodyP}>
    On Unix systems, you need to{" "}
    <a href="https://unix.stackexchange.com/a/117470/101951" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={linkInline}>find your shell profile file</a>,
    and then add to the end of this file the following line reflecting the path
    to your Elixir installation:
  </p>

  <pre class={codeBlock} tabindex="0">export PATH="$PATH:/path/to/elixir/bin"</pre>
</div>
